Stops a recording the moment it's asked to, and keeps what it took.
wf-recorder asks the compositor for each frame with damage, which comes
only once something on the screen moves, and waits for it in
wl_display_dispatch, whose poll goes on waiting when a signal breaks in.
So SIGINT set the flag to stop, but nothing read it until the next
frame: over a still screen, up to a minute later, and the recording
wasn't saved until then. The signal now also writes to an eventfd the
wait polls beside the display, so the wait gives way at once whichever
thread took the signal, and even when it came just before the wait
began. Stopping at once left two more gaps, each of which emptied a
short recording: the writer left at the stop without encoding frames
already captured, and over a still screen the only frame was the first,
of no length, so nothing played. The writer now encodes every captured
frame before it leaves, and a stop takes one last frame without damage,
which the compositor draws at once, so the recording runs to the stop
and ends on what was shown then. Laid over
wf-recorder-dmabuf-version.patch.

